--
libstdc++ 13 <sstream>: `o << 4' leaves o.str() empty.  Diagnosed (rounds
163v-w): basic_ostream<char>::_M_insert<long> is declared `extern
template' in bits/ostream.tcc ([temp.explicit]/12), so its body is not
instantiated, and provide_stdlib_bodies replaces the bodyless instance by
a model that only returns *this ([ostream.inserters.arithmetic]/1 requires
the insertion).  Instantiating it instead (an experiment, not kept) fails
next on `this->_M_num_put': basic_ostream<char> is instantiated eagerly
from within basic_ios<char> (basic_ios.h:88 names ostreambuf_iterator,
whose typedef names basic_ostream, [temp.inst]/2 requires neither), while
basic_ios<char>, its virtual base, has only its ios_base members, and
basic_ostream<char> keeps that partial member list.  Re-elaborating the
derived class once the base is complete crashed on its stale scope.  The
virtual base's default member initializers are fixed
(cpp11_virtual_base_default_member_initializer).  g++ 13 accepts this
program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
